H6300.definition:
from H6299 (פָּדָה) and H410 (אֵל); God has ransomed;
Pedahel, an Israelite
KJV: Pedahel.

H6301.definition:
from H6299 (פָּדָה) and H6697 (צוּר); a rock (i.e. God) has ransomed;
Pedahtsur, an Israelite
KJV: Pedahzur.

H6302.definition:
passive participle of H6299 (פָּדָה). ransomed (and so occurring under H6299 (פָּדָה));
as abstractly (in plural masculine) a ransom
KJV: (that are) to be (that were) redeemed.

H6303.definition:
from H6299 (פָּדָה); ransom;
Padon, one of the Nethinim.
KJV: Padon.

H6304.definition:
or פְּדֻת; from H6929 (קֵדְמָה)lemma קדְמָה missing vowel, corrected to קֵדְמָה;
distinction; also deliverance
KJV: division, redeem, redemption.

H6305.definition:
or פְּדָיָהוּ; from H6299 (פָּדָה) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has ransomed;
Pedajah, the name of six Israelites
KJV: Pedaiah.

H6306.definition:
or פִּדְיֹם; also פִּדְיוֹן; or פִּדְיֹן; from H6299 (פָּדָה);
a ransom
KJV: ransom, that were redeemed, redemption.

H6307.definition:
from an unused root meaning to extend; a plateau; or פַּדַּן אֲרָם; from the same and H758 (אֲרָם); the table-land of Aram;
Paddan or Paddan-Aram, a region of Syria
KJV: Padan, Padan-aram.

H6308.definition:
a primitive root;
to retrieve
KJV: deliver.

H6309.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be greasy;
suet
KJV: fat.

H6310.definition:
from H6284 (פָּאָה);
the mouth (as the means of blowing), whether literal or figurative (particularly speech); specifically edge, portion or side; adverbially (with preposition) according to
KJV: accord(-ing as, -ing to), after, appointment, assent, collar, command(-ment), [idiom] eat, edge, end, entry, [phrase] file, hole, [idiom] in, mind, mouth, part, portion, [idiom] (should) say(-ing), sentence, skirt, sound, speech, [idiom] spoken, talk, tenor, [idiom] to, [phrase] two-edged, wish, word.

H6311.definition:
or פֹּא; (Job 38:11), or פּוֹ; probably from a primitive inseparable particle 'p' (of demonstrative force) and H1931 (הוּא);
this place (French ici), i.e. here or hence
KJV: here, hither, the one (other, this, that) side.

H6312.definition:
or פֻּוָּה; from H6284 (פָּאָה); a blast;
Puah or Puvvah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Phuvah, Pua, Puah.

H6313.definition:
a primitive root;
to be sluggish
KJV: cease, be feeble, faint, be slacked.

H6315.definition:
a primitive root;
to puff, i.e. blow with the breath or air; hence, to fan (as a breeze), to utter, to kindle (a fire), to scoff
KJV: blow (upon), break, puff, bring into a snare, speak, utter.

H6316.definition:
of foreign origin;
Put, a son of Ham, also the name of his descendants or their region, and of a Persian tribe
KJV: Phut, Put.

H6317.definition:
from an unused root (probably meaning to disparage) and H410 (אֵל); contempt of God;
Putiel, an Israelite
KJV: Putiel.

H6318.definition:
of Egyptian derivation;
Potiphar, an Egyptian
KJV: Potiphar.

H6319.definition:
of Egyptian derivation;
Poti-Phera, an Egyptian
KJV: Poti-pherah.

H6320.definition:
from an unused root meaning to paint;
dye (specifically, stibium for the eyes)
KJV: fair colours, glistering, paint(-ed) (-ing).

H6321.definition:
from an unused root meaning to be thick;
a bean (as plump)
KJV: beans.

H6322.definition:
of foreign origin;
Pul, the name of an Assyrian king and of an Ethiopian tribe
KJV: Pul.

H6324.definition:
patronymically from an unused name meaning a turn;
a Punite (collectively) or descendants of an unknown Pun
KJV: Punites.

H6325.definition:
from H6323 (פּוּן); perplexity;
Punon, a place in the Desert
KJV: Punon.

H6326.definition:
from an unused root meaning to glitter; brilliancy;
Puah, an Israelitess
KJV: Puah.

H6327.definition:
a primitive root;
to dash in pieces, literally or figuratively (especially to disperse)
KJV: break (dash, shake) in (to) pieces, cast (abroad), disperse (selves), drive, retire, scatter (abroad), spread abroad.

H6328.definition:
a primitive root;
to waver
KJV: stumble, move.

H6329.definition:
a primitive root (identical with H6328 (פּוּק) through the idea of dropping out; compare H5312 (נְפַק));
to issue, i.e. furnish; causatively, to secure; figuratively, to succeed
KJV: afford, draw out, further, get, obtain.

H6330.definition:
from H6328 (פּוּק);
a stumbling-block
KJV: grief.

H6331.definition:
a primitive root;
to crush
KJV: break, bring to nought, [idiom] utterly take.

H6332.definition:
also (plural) פּוּרִים; or פֻּרִים; from H6331 (פּוּר);
a lot (as by means of a broken piece)
KJV: Pur, Purim.

H6333.definition:
from H6331 (פּוּר);
a wine-press (as crushing the grapes)
KJV: winepress.

H6334.definition:
of Persian origin;
Poratha, a son of Haman
KJV: Poratha.

H6335.definition:
a primitive root;
to spread; figuratively, act proudly
KJV: grow up, be grown fat, spread selves, be scattered.

H6336.definition:
patronymically from an unused name meaning a hinge;
a Puthite (collectively) or descendants of an unknown Puth
KJV: Puhites (as if from H6312 (פּוּאָה)).

H6337.definition:
from H6338 (פָּזַז);
pure (gold); hence, gold itself (as refined)
KJV: fine (pure) gold.

H6338.definition:
a primitive root;
to refine (gold)
KJV: best (gold).

H6339.definition:
a primitive root (identical with H6338 (פָּזַז));
to solidify (as if by refining); also to spring (as if separating the limbs)
KJV: leap, be made strong.

H6340.definition:
a primitive root;
to scatter, whether in enmity or bounty
KJV: disperse, scatter (abroad).

H6341.definition:
from H6351 (פָּחַח);
a (metallic) sheet (as pounded thin); also a spring net (as spread out like a lamina)
KJV: gin, (thin) plate, snare.

H6342.definition:
a primitive root;
to be startled (by a sudden alarm); hence, to fear in general
KJV: be afraid, stand in awe, (be in) fear, make to shake.

H6343.definition:
from H6342 (פָּחַד);
a (sudden) alarm (properly, the object feared, by implication, the feeling)
KJV: dread(-ful), fear, (thing) great (fear, -ly feared), terror.

H6344.definition:
the same as H6343 (פַּחַד);
a testicle (as a cause of shame akin to fear)
KJV: stone.

H6345.definition:
feminine of H6343 (פַּחַד);
alarm (i.e. awe)
KJV: fear.

H6346.definition:
of foreign origin;
a prefect (of a city or small district)
KJV: captain, deputy, governor.

H6347.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6346 (פֶּחָה)
{a prefect (of a city or small district)}
KJV: captain, governor.

H6348.definition:
a primitive root;
to bubble up or froth (as boiling water), i.e. (figuratively) to be unimportant
KJV: light.

H6349.definition:
from H6348 (פָּחַז);
ebullition, i.e. froth (figuratively, lust)
KJV: unstable.

H6352.definition:
perhaps from an unused root probably meaning to be black;
a coal, whether charred or live
KJV: coals.

H6353.definition:
(Aramaic) from an unused root probably meaning to fashion;
a potter
KJV: potter.

H6354.definition:
probably from an unused root apparently meaning to dig;
a pit, especially forcatching animals
KJV: hole, pit, snare.

H6355.definition:
from H6354 (פַּחַת) and H4124 (מוֹאָב); pit of Moab;
Pachath-Moab, an Israelite
KJV: Pahathmoab.

H6356.definition:
from the same as H6354 (פַּחַת);
a hole (by mildew in a garment)
KJV: fret inward.

H6357.definition:
of foreign derivation;
a gem, probably the topaz
KJV: topaz.

H6358.definition:
passive participle of H6362 (פָּטַר);
opened, i.e. (as noun) a bud
KJV: open.

H6359.definition:
from H6362 (פָּטַר);
open, i.e. unoccupied
KJV: free.

H6360.definition:
intensively from an unused root meaning to pound;
a hammer
KJV: hammer.

H6361.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to that of H6360 (פַּטִּישׁ);
a gown (as if hammered out wide)
KJV: hose.

H6362.definition:
a primitive root;
to cleave or burst through, i.e. (causatively) to emit, whether literal or figurative (gape)
KJV: dismiss, free, let (shoot) out, slip away.

H6363.definition:
or פִּטְרָה; from H6362 (פָּטַר);
a fissure, i.e. (concretely) firstling (as opening the matrix)
KJV: firstling, openeth, such as open.

H6364.definition:
of Egyptian origin;
Pi-Beseth, a place in Egypt
KJV: Pi-beseth.

H6365.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to pierce;
(figuratively) misfortune
KJV: destruction, ruin.

H6366.definition:
or פִּיָּה; feminine of H6310 (פֶּה);
an edge
KJV: (two-) edge(-d).

H6367.definition:
from H6310 (פֶּה) and the feminine plural of a noun (from the same root as H2356 (חוֹר)), with the article interpolated; mouth of the gorges;
Pi-ha-Chiroth, a place in Egypt
KJV: Pi-hahiroth. (In Numbers 14:19 without Pi-.)

H6368.definition:
from H6315 (פּוּחַ);
a powder (as easily puffed away), i.e. ashes or dust
KJV: ashes.

H6369.definition:
apparently from H6310 (פֶּה) and H3605 (כֹּל); mouth of all;
Picol, a Philistine
KJV: Phichol.

H6370.definition:
or פִּלֶגֶשׁ; of uncertain derivation;
a concubine; also (masculine) a paramour
KJV: concubine, paramour.

H6371.definition:
probably from an unused root meaning to be plump;
obesity
KJV: collops.

H6372.definition:
apparently from H6310 (פֶּה) and a variation of H5175 (נָחָשׁ); mouth of a serpent;
Pinechas, the name of three Israelites
KJV: Phinehas.

H6373.definition:
probably the same as H6325 (פּוּנֹן);
Pinon, an Idumaean
KJV: Pinon.

H6374.definition:
for H6366 (פֵּיָה);
an edge or tooth
KJV: tooth, [idiom] two-edged.

H6375.definition:
from H6329 (פּוּק);
a tottering
KJV: smite together.

H6376.definition:
from H6335 (פּוּשׁ); dispersive;
Pishon, a river of Eden
KJV: Pison.

H6377.definition:
probably from the same as H6596 (פֹּת); expansive;
Pithon, an Israelite
KJV: Pithon.

H6378.definition:
from H6379 (פָּכָה);
a flask (from which a liquid may flow)
KJV: box, vial.

H6379.definition:
a primitive root;
to pour
KJV: run out.

H6380.definition:
from the active participle (of the same form as the first word) feminine of an unused root (meaning to entrap) and plural of H6643 (צְבִי); trap of gazelles;
Pokereth-Tsebajim, one of the 'servants of Solomon'
KJV: Pochereth of Zebaim.

H6381.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, perhaps to separate, i.e. distinguish (literally or figuratively); by implication, to be (causatively, make) great, difficult, wonderful
KJV: accomplish, (arise...too, be too) hard, hidden, things too high, (be, do, do a, shew) marvelous(-ly, -els, things, work), miracles, perform, separate, make singular, (be, great, make) wonderful(-ers, -ly, things, works), wondrous (things, works, -ly).

H6382.definition:
from H6381 (פָּלָא);
a miracle
KJV: marvellous thing, wonder(-ful, -fully).

H6383.definition:
or פָּלִיא; from H6381 (פָּלָא);
remarkable
KJV: secret, wonderful.

H6384.definition:
patronymically from H6396 (פַּלּוּא);
a Palluite (collectively) or descendants of Pallu
KJV: Palluites.

H6385.definition:
a primitive root;
to split (literally or figuratively)
KJV: divide.

H6386.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6385 (פָּלַג)
{to split (literally or figuratively)}
KJV: divided.

H6387.definition:
(Aramaic) from H6386 (פְּלַג);
a half
KJV: dividing.

H6388.definition:
from H6385 (פָּלַג);
a rill (i.e. small channel of water, as in irrigation)
KJV: river, stream.

H6389.definition:
the same as H6388 (פֶּלֶג); earthquake;
Peleg, a son of Shem
KJV: Peleg.

H6390.definition:
from H6385 (פָּלַג);
a runlet, i.e. gully
KJV: division, river.

H6391.definition:
from H6385 (פָּלַג);
a section
KJV: division.

H6392.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6391 (פְּלֻגָּה)
{a section}
KJV: division.

H6393.definition:
from an unused root meaning to divide;
a cleaver, i.e. iron armature (of a chariot)
KJV: torch.

H6394.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Pildash, a relative of Abraham
KJV: Pildash.

H6395.definition:
a primitive root;
to distinguish (literally or figuratively)
KJV: put a difference, show marvellous, separate, set apart, sever, make wonderfully.

H6396.definition:
from H6395 (פָּלָה); distinguished;
Pallu, an Israelite
KJV: Pallu, Phallu.

H6397.definition:
patronymically from an unused name (from H6395 (פָּלָה)) meaning separate;
a Pelonite or inhabitant of an unknown Palon
KJV: Pelonite.

H6398.definition:
a primitive root;
to slice, i.e. break open or pierce
KJV: bring forth, cleave, cut, shred, strike through.

H6399.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H6398 (פָּלַח);
to serve or worship
KJV: minister, serve.
